  <h2>Gotchas for cmd users</h2>
  <ul class="gotchas">
    <li><strong>Switches use a dash, not a slash.</strong> <code>dir /s</code> becomes <code>Get-ChildItem -Recurse</code>. <code>dir</code> still works as an alias, but <code>/s</code> does not.</li>
    <li><strong>Variables:</strong> <code>%USERPROFILE%</code> becomes <code>$env:USERPROFILE</code>. Set one with <code>$env:NAME = 'value'</code>; it lasts until you close the window.</li>
    <li><strong>Run a program in the current folder with <code>.\</code></strong>, for example <code>.\setup.exe</code>. PowerShell does not look in the current folder on its own.</li>
    <li><strong>Paths with spaces need quotes and <code>&amp;</code></strong> to run: <code>&amp; 'C:\Program Files\App\app.exe'</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Old tools still work.</strong> <code>ipconfig</code>, <code>ping</code>, <code>robocopy</code>, and <code>netstat</code> run fine from PowerShell. They return text instead of objects.</li>
    <li><strong>Batch files (<code>.bat</code>, <code>.cmd</code>) still run</strong>, but scripts (<code>.ps1</code>) follow the <a href="/guides/execution-policy/">execution policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

